@startuml Order Placement with Stock Locking
!theme plain
title Order Placement with Stock Locking\n(Transaction-Safe Order Creation with Row-Level Locks)

' Participants
actor Customer as customer #LightBlue
participant "OrderController" as controller #E3F2FD
participant "OrderService" as orderService #E3F2FD
participant "CartService" as cartService #E3F2FD
participant "ProductService" as productService #E3F2FD
participant "StockService" as stockService #E3F2FD
participant "PaymentService" as paymentService #E3F2FD
database "Database\n(Transactional)" as db #E8F5E9
participant "EventSystem" as eventSystem #FCE4EC

' Main Flow
customer -> controller: POST /api/v1/orders\n{checkout_token: "chk_xyz123"}
activate controller

controller -> orderService: createOrder(checkoutSession)
activate orderService

' Checkout Session Validation
orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM checkout_sessions\nWHERE token = 'chk_xyz123'\nAND expires_at > NOW()
activate db
db --> orderService: CheckoutSession\n{cart_id: 5, user_id: 42, expires_at: "2025-01-01 10:30:00"}
deactivate db

alt Checkout Session Valid
    ' Load Cart
    orderService -> cartService: getCart(5)
    activate cartService
    
    cartService -> db: SELECT * FROM carts WHERE id = 5
    activate db
    db --> cartService: Cart {id: 5, user_id: 42, status: 'active'}
    deactivate db
    
    cartService -> db: SELECT * FROM cart_items WHERE cart_id = 5
    activate db
    db --> cartService: CartItems [3 items]
    deactivate db
    
    cartService --> orderService: Cart with items:\n[{product_id: 10, quantity: 2},\n {product_id: 15, quantity: 1},\n {product_id: 20, quantity: 5}]
    deactivate cartService
    
    ' ===== BEGIN TRANSACTION =====
    orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    activate db #FFCCCC
    note over db
        **🔒 TRANSACTION STARTS**
        All operations below are atomic
        Rollback on any error
    end note
    
    ' ===== PRE-ORDER VALIDATION =====
    group Pre-Order Validation (Inside Transaction)
        orderService -> cartService: validateCart(cart)
        activate cartService
        
        loop For each cart item
            cartService -> productService: getProduct(product_id)
            activate productService
            productService -> db: SELECT * FROM products WHERE id = ?
            db --> productService: Product {id, name, price, is_active, stock_quantity}
            productService --> cartService: Product
            deactivate productService
            
            alt Product inactive or deleted
                cartService -> cartService: Add validation error:\n"Product {name} is no longer available"
            else Product price changed
                cartService -> cartService: Add validation warning:\n"Price updated from $X to $Y"
            end
            
            cartService -> stockService: checkStock(product_id, quantity)
            activate stockService
            stockService -> db: SELECT stock_quantity FROM products WHERE id = ?
            db --> stockService: stock_quantity
            
            alt Stock insufficient
                stockService --> cartService: {available: false, current_stock: X}
                cartService -> cartService: Add validation error:\n"Only X items available for {product}"
            else Stock sufficient
                stockService --> cartService: {available: true}
            end
            deactivate stockService
        end
        
        alt Validation has errors
            cartService --> orderService: ValidationResult {valid: false, errors: [...]}
            deactivate cartService
            
            orderService -> db: ROLLBACK
            note over db
                **🔓 TRANSACTION ROLLED BACK**
                No changes committed
            end note
            deactivate db
            
            orderService --> controller: Validation errors
            deactivate orderService
            
            controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::error(\n  errors,\n  'Cart validation failed',\n  422\n)
            deactivate controller
        else Validation successful
            cartService --> orderService: ValidationResult {valid: true}
            deactivate cartService
        end
    end
    
    ' ===== STOCK LOCKING & DEDUCTION =====
    group Stock Locking & Deduction (Critical Section)
        note over orderService, stockService
            **🔒 ROW-LEVEL LOCKS ACQUIRED**
            Sequential locking prevents deadlocks
            Locks held until transaction commits
        end note
        
        loop For each cart item (in ascending product_id order)
            orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM products\nWHERE id = ?\nFOR UPDATE
            note right of db
                **FOR UPDATE:**
                - Acquires exclusive row lock
                - Blocks other transactions
                - Prevents concurrent stock deduction
                - Released on COMMIT/ROLLBACK
            end note
            db --> orderService: Product (🔒 LOCKED)
            
            orderService -> stockService: deductStock(\n  product_id,\n  quantity,\n  reference_type: 'order',\n  reference_id: null // Not created yet\n)
            activate stockService
            
            stockService -> db: UPDATE products\nSET stock_quantity = stock_quantity - ?\nWHERE id = ?
            db --> stockService: Rows affected: 1
            
            stockService -> db: INSERT INTO stock_movements\n(product_id, type: 'deduction', quantity: -X,\nreference_type: 'order', notes: 'Order placement')
            db --> stockService: stock_movement.id created
            
            stockService --> orderService: Success {new_stock: Y}
            deactivate stockService
            
            note over db
                Product {id} stock locked and deducted
                Lock still held until transaction ends
            end note
        end
    end
    
    ' ===== ORDER CREATION =====
    group Order & Related Records Creation
        orderService -> orderService: generateOrderNumber()
        note right of orderService
            **Order Number Format:**
            ORD-{YYYYMMDD}-{SEQUENCE}
            Example: ORD-20250101-00001
            
            Configurable via:
            config('arkenstone.order_number_prefix')
        end note
        orderService --> orderService: order_number = "ORD-20250101-00001"
        
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO orders\n(\n  order_number,\n  user_id,\n  cart_id,\n  status: 'pending_payment',\n  payment_status: 'pending',\n  payment_method,\n  subtotal,\n  tax_amount,\n  shipping_cost,\n  discount_amount,\n  grand_total,\n  currency: 'USD'\n)
        db --> orderService: order.id = 123
        
        ' Create Order Items
        loop For each cart item
            orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM products WHERE id = ?
            db --> orderService: Product (full details)
            
            orderService -> orderService: Create product snapshot:\n{\n  "id": 10,\n  "name": "Product Name",\n  "sku": "SKU-123",\n  "price": 29.99,\n  "image": "...",\n  "attributes": {...}\n}
            
            orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_items\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  product_id,\n  product_sku,\n  product_name,\n  quantity,\n  unit_price,\n  discount_type,\n  discount_value,\n  discount_amount,\n  tax_rate,\n  tax_amount,\n  subtotal,\n  total_price,\n  product_snapshot: JSON\n)
            db --> orderService: order_item.id created
            
            note right of db
                **Product Snapshot:**
                Preserves product data at order time
                Order history remains accurate even if:
                - Product deleted
                - Price changed
                - Attributes modified
            end note
        end
        
        ' Create Shipping Address
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_shipping_addresses\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  full_name,\n  phone,\n  email,\n  address_line_1,\n  address_line_2,\n  city,\n  state,\n  postal_code,\n  country,\n  latitude,\n  longitude\n)
        db --> orderService: shipping_address.id created
        
        ' Create Billing Address
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_billing_addresses\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  full_name,\n  phone,\n  email,\n  address_line_1,\n  city,\n  state,\n  postal_code,\n  country\n)
        db --> orderService: billing_address.id created
        
        ' Update Cart Status
        orderService -> db: UPDATE carts\nSET status = 'completed',\norder_id = 123,\ncompleted_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 5
        db --> orderService: Cart updated
        
        ' Create Initial Status History
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  from_status: NULL,\n  to_status: 'pending_payment',\n  changed_by_type: 'customer',\n  changed_by: 42,\n  note: 'Order created'\n)
        db --> orderService: status_history created
        
        ' Update stock_movements with order_id
        orderService -> db: UPDATE stock_movements\nSET reference_id = 123\nWHERE reference_type = 'order'\nAND created_at > ? // Last 5 seconds
        db --> orderService: Stock movements linked
    end
    
    ' ===== COMMIT TRANSACTION =====
    orderService -> db: COMMIT
    note over db
        **✅ TRANSACTION COMMITTED**
        All changes persisted atomically:
        - Stock deducted and locked
        - Order and items created
        - Addresses saved
        - Cart marked completed
        - Status history recorded
        
        **🔓 ALL LOCKS RELEASED**
    end note
    deactivate db
    
    ' ===== POST-TRANSACTION OPERATIONS =====
    group Post-Transaction (After Commit)
        ' Dispatch Events
        orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.created', order)
        activate eventSystem
        note over eventSystem
            **Event Listeners:**
            - Send order confirmation notification
            - Update admin dashboard
            - Trigger analytics tracking
            - Log to audit trail
        end note
        eventSystem ->> eventSystem: Async event processing
        deactivate eventSystem
        
        ' Payment Method Branching
        alt Payment Method = COD
            orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET status = 'confirmed',\npayment_status = 'cod_pending',\nconfirmed_at = NOW()
            
            orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(from_status: 'pending_payment', to_status: 'confirmed')
            
            orderService -> db: INSERT INTO payments\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  payment_method: 'cod',\n  status: 'cod_pending',\n  amount: grand_total,\n  currency: 'USD'\n)
            
            orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.confirmed', order)
            
            orderService --> controller: Order\n{status: 'confirmed', payment_method: 'cod'}
            deactivate orderService
            
            controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  order,\n  'Order confirmed! Pay on delivery'\n)
            deactivate controller
            
        else Payment Method = BANK_TRANSFER
            orderService -> db: INSERT INTO payments\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  payment_method: 'bank_transfer',\n  status: 'awaiting_payment',\n  amount: grand_total\n)
            
            orderService --> controller: Order\n{status: 'pending_payment', bank_details: {...}}
            deactivate orderService
            
            controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  {order, bank_details},\n  'Transfer to bank account within 48h'\n)
            deactivate controller
            
        else Payment Method = CARD
            orderService -> paymentService: initiatePayment(order)
            activate paymentService
            note over paymentService
                **See Payment Processing Diagram**
                - Creates payment record
                - Calls payment gateway adapter
                - Returns redirect URL
            end note
            paymentService --> orderService: Payment {redirect_url: "..."}
            deactivate paymentService
            
            orderService --> controller: Order {redirect_url: "..."}
            deactivate orderService
            
            controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  {order, redirect_url},\n  'Complete payment to confirm order'\n)
            deactivate controller
        end
    end
    
else Checkout Session Invalid/Expired
    orderService --> controller: CheckoutSessionExpired error
    deactivate orderService
    
    controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::error(\n  null,\n  'Checkout session expired. Please restart checkout.',\n  422\n)
    deactivate controller
end

' Notes
note over db
    **Transaction Isolation Level:**
    READ COMMITTED (Laravel default)
    
    **Deadlock Prevention:**
    - Lock products in ascending ID order
    - Keep transaction duration minimal
    - Use row-level locks (not table locks)
    
    **Rollback Scenarios:**
    - Validation failure
    - Insufficient stock
    - Constraint violation
    - Database error
    All operations reversed automatically
end note

note over orderService, stockService
    **Why Row-Level Locks?**
    
    Without locks (Race Condition):
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ Transaction A reads stock: 5 items  │
    │ Transaction B reads stock: 5 items  │ ← Both see 5
    │ Transaction A deducts 3 → stock: 2  │
    │ Transaction B deducts 3 → stock: 2  │ ← WRONG! Should be -1
    └─────────────────────────────────────┘
    
    With FOR UPDATE locks:
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ Transaction A locks & reads: 5      │
    │ Transaction B waits... (blocked)    │ ← Lock prevents read
    │ Transaction A deducts 3 → stock: 2  │
    │ Transaction A commits (lock released)│
    │ Transaction B locks & reads: 2      │ ← Now sees correct value
    │ Transaction B deducts 3 → FAILS     │ ← Validation catches error
    └─────────────────────────────────────┘
end note

note over customer, controller
    **Order Flow Summary:**
    
    1️⃣ Validate checkout session (not expired)
    2️⃣ Load cart and items
    3️⃣ 🔒 BEGIN TRANSACTION
    4️⃣ Re-validate all items (stock/price/availability)
    5️⃣ Lock products sequentially (FOR UPDATE)
    6️⃣ Deduct stock with stock_movements logging
    7️⃣ Create order with generated order_number
    8️⃣ Create order_items with product snapshots
    9️⃣ Copy shipping & billing addresses
    🔟 Mark cart as completed
    1️⃣1️⃣ ✅ COMMIT (all or nothing)
    1️⃣2️⃣ Dispatch events
    1️⃣3️⃣ Branch by payment method
    
    **Duration:** ~500ms for 10 items
end note

@enduml
